Changes by We Meet (2026-10-10):
- Retained only six encoder classes and two mel preprocessing functions.
- Removed all language-model, tokenizer, network and speech-generation code.
- Replaced the configuration type with an immutable local dataclass containing
  the pinned official speaker encoder defaults.
- Removed waveform-derived warning prints; acceptance is checked separately.
- Imports are limited to Torch, librosa mel and the local configuration.

No encoder forward or mel formula was changed. Float32 inference and subsequent
L2 normalization are explicit We Meet feature-space rules. Qwen's model card
declares Apache-2.0 for the pinned model weights; the artifact manifest records
the exact upstream revision and whole-file checksum independently of this code.
